{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Our shield</b> — it is the king who shields through the hand of the people, as in: 'for to YHWH is our shield' (Psalms 33:20). The meaning is that HaShem will deliver our king, for in his days the festal pilgrims will go to the House of HaShem without fear of the enemy."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 84, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:59.349167102Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}